WEBVTT

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.240
Sidekick!

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.920
You are the most burdensome sidekick ever.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.170
Your "it's whatever" act towards me
feels pretty forced at this point.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:01.970
Episode 6

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:11.150
Siesta... How did you...
procure such a thing?

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.900
Oh, it was just kind of...
lying abandoned in the street?

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.620
Don't lie! No way something like
this was lying by the roadside.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.830
I'm telling you, it's true!

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.710
There's certainly no way that I got
so disturbed at your being abducted

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.040
that I vigorously wrangled
with the government

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:32.880
to borrow Sirius, a humanoid weapon
that had been in covert development.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.220
You've been busier than I thought.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:41.720
Siesta, you were too,
too desperate to save me.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.890
I told you, that's not what happened.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.390
This is too much.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:52.150
The way you're going back and forth
so heatedly with my future partner...

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.070
...I'm getting jealous.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.280
Hel, why are you fomenting
this sort of terrorism?

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:07.080
Why? It's because it's my destiny.
I merely abide by the Sacred Writ.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.460
No. What I'm asking about
is your own intent.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.590
My intent? That's what I mean--

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:18.430
it's to bring about the future
that's inscribed in the Sacred Writ.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:21.640
That alone is the meaning of my existence.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.600
I was born only for that purpose.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.650
Is that so? But still...

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:33.820
I won't let you go any further
with your designs for this city.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:38.990
Do you truly believe you can stop me?

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.740
Stop destiny?

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:43.870
Sidekick!

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.870
So cramped...

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:54.960
Well, it's made to seat one.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.670
If you take advantage of this as a chance
to touch somewhere unseemly,

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.880
you'll earn my full contempt.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.220
Do you have zero faith in your sidekick?

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:14.190
Right, here we go. Sirius, charge!

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.200
I never dreamed you'd gone so far
as to create a monster like this.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.460
And as for you, you needlessly impede us.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:31.210
That's because it's my mission.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:43.510
Siesta!

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:47.640
It's fine, I won't let them
get away. Hold on.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.590
Rocket... hands!

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:22.510
Shouldn't that tone of voice
be used to say "punch"?

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.390
Is there a problem here?

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.060
You're just too, too persistent.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:41.610
You said something earlier...
Impeding us was your mission, you said.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:47.700
So why do you work as a detective?
Why do you protect people?

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:53.290
It's because you were born for that
particular existence, nothing more.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.590
It's the same. I'm the same.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:05.300
Just as you were born to defend the world,
I was born to destroy the world.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:09.560
I'm merely obeying the instincts
I was born with.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.850
So you're saying that we're,
in essence, the same,

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.810
and what's more, that there's no
difference between good and evil?

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:20.320
A difference between good and evil?
It doesn't matter to me if there is one.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:25.280
You're good, I'm evil--
that's fine with me.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:28.280
I can live with that.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.590
Siesta!

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:41.800
Sidekick...

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:42.960
Now we fly.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.220
Eh?

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.930
Engines, full throttle!

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.360
Can't allow that!

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.080
Sidekick...

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.380
Whatever happens after this,
clear out of this place immediately.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:21.090
Siesta, what are you saying?

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:29.260
Siesta... why?

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:46.820
Siesta!

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:01.920
Siesta... Hey, where are you, Siesta?

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.880
Are you stupid or something?

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:13.260
You had no right to say anything before.
You're way too desperate about me, Kimi.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:23.020
I'm positive I told you before,
whatever happens, to clear out immed--

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.820
You're the stupid one.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:32.530
Why did you act so recklessly?
Why did you send me away?

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:39.460
It was purely as a last resort.
I had no intention of dying here either.

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:44.460
But if only one of us could
survive, in that case, I--

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.880
Stop that nonsense!

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:53.390
Listen, three years ago, on that plane,
you asked me to join you.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:58.640
That being so, you need to look
after me, till the bitter end!

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:03.440
Sorry, but in your absence, I have no
confidence I can escape from SPES.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:10.070
I can't survive without you!
Do you understand? If you do...

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:14.370
...live up to your obligations
to the very end and protect me!

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:21.250
In my entire life, this is the first time
anyone's ever shouted at me this much.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:28.380
So you do get worked up like this.
What can I say...?

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.420
It makes me smile.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:35.430
It makes you smile?

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:38.270
"I can't survive without you," huh?

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:41.390
Hey, stop cherry-picking peculiar
phrases out of context.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:44.730
Once again I've been hit
with an ardent proposal.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:47.770
I haven't proposed!

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:51.610
Well, once you turn 18,
give it another try.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:56.320
I told you I-- Whatever.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:09:59.910
I vow to you...

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.200
Eh?

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:08.000
I won't go off and willfully die without
saying a word to you. Absolutely not.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:13.760
Sidekick!

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.470
Not yet...

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:27.310
I can't die yet.

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:28.730
Hel.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:33.530
It's not my destiny...
to die in a place like this.

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:38.580
I'm the one who wins in the end. If not...

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:42.200
The significance Father gave
to me respective to this...

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:46.330
I see, you...

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:52.760
With this, I'll finish it. You won't be
able to move a single step from there...

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:55.470
...and my blade will run you through.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.100
Get out of the way, Siesta!

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:03.890
Hel's power... Siesta!

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:22.580
How...?

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.710
Checkmate.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:38.800
Why... did I lose...?

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:44.680
This wasn't supposed to...
I had a mission...

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:49.150
Was fighting for a mission... A mission...

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:55.900
Why was I born? Why was I...?

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:01.530
Find your answers in Hell.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.490
Chameleon!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.370
A partner?

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.590
I won't let her escape!

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:20.220
Her body vanished...

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:23.390
Probably a power of the partner
she just called out to.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:26.180
Chameleon...

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.680
Sidekick...

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:32.440
I'm sorry.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.670
These apples aren't very juicy.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.790
Don't complain when I'm handfeeding you.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.590
There's no way around that, right?
Since I injured myself.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:01.180
Your leg, yes. Your hands
are available, right?

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:06.510
In the desperate battle of a few
days before, during a fall,

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:10.980
Siesta sustained a leg injury that will
take a couple of weeks to fully heal.

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:15.270
Ordinarily, we'd have needed
to pursue Hel in all haste,

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:19.190
but with Siesta like this,
there's nothing to be done.

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:22.070
Are you all right, Kimi?

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:27.370
Taking diligent care of a self-indulgent
partner like this doesn't faze me.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:29.500
Oh? That's good.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:32.330
Don't ignore the sarcasm
I put so much effort into.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:36.630
I'm fine, but hurry up and recover from
that. I'm no good at domestic work.

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:39.630
We're living together,
just as you've dreamed of.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.010
Shouldn't you enjoy it just a little?

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:45.350
Don't call it "living together."
It's a tactical bunking-up.

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:49.390
Also, it's good that you improve
your practical life skills a little.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:52.020
What will you do when I'm gone?

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:54.980
Hey, that's off-limits.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:58.360
That's right; I'm going to
get shouted at again.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.530
Are you going out?

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:04.450
You'd prefer juicier ones, right?

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:11.040
What? Why are you laughing?

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.580
Kimi... you like me too,
too much, don't you?

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:21.920
Huh? I don't know what you mean...
Huh? No, just... Wha--?

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:25.890
I had no idea you'd get so flustered.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:30.060
Shut up, you ignoramus!

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:39.440
Cripes. I'm not going
to spoil her ever again.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:49.330
Huh?

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:59.420
What to do...

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:11.770
It's been a while since I've gotten
caught up in a mundane problem like this.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:24.490
Oh...

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:25.740
Hm?

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:30.870
I'm going to be attacked.

00:15:30.870 --> 00:15:32.540
Huh?

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.330
I'm going to be attacked.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:41.840
I've got an intensely bad feeling
about this, but I guess I'll ask.

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.590
Who are you going to be attacked by?

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:46.760
By you!

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.760
However, you might have
your way with me physically,

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:52.140
but if you think you can also take control
of my heart, you're very mistaken!

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:56.850
And I'm immediately hit with
baseless suspicions. This is absurd.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:01.360
Sorry, but I'm not interested in children.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:03.730
Who are you calling a child?!

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:08.660
Now, now. Cool down a little.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:11.780
In this type of situation,
introductions would be a good start.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:17.120
My name is Kimihiko Kimizuka.
What's yours?

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:20.000
I'm...

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.960
...Alicia?

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:26.550
Why was that in question form? Did you
come from Wonderland or something?

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:28.300
I'm hungry.

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:32.680
This conversation is really
lacking in continuity.

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:37.180
Are they good?

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:40.560
Yeah, they're delicious--really sweet!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:46.320
That's--! Did you eat all of those?

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:49.450
So, where are we?

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:54.660
"Where are we?" Didn't you choose
this yourself as a place to sleep?

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.250
I don't know.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.420
Amnesia...

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:02.880
Eh?

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:05.090
Is there anything you remember?

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:11.640
I only remember that I'm
17 years old as of this year.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:14.720
Hurry up and forget that because
you've definitely got that wrong.

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:18.730
Where are you looking
when you say that?

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:22.980
I took her for an ordinary runaway,

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:26.150
but this seems more
complicated than I thought.

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.900
For starters, we're going to the police.

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:48.340
Sidekick? Are you back?

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:53.300
Uh, yeah. And what are you doing?

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:55.930
I thought I'd make apple pie,

00:17:55.930 --> 00:18:00.140
since you said you were going out
just to buy more for me.

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:05.610
Ah. Um, so, Siesta... It's just...

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:10.070
Since you seem to care
about me quite a bit,

00:18:10.070 --> 00:18:12.950
call it a sense of obligation,
as a crush-ee.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:16.240
I thought I'd do this much for you.

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:20.200
So where are the apples?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.080
Umm, the thing is...

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.080
Kimizuka!

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:30.130
Aren't there any smaller towels?

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.270
You lolicon.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:47.980
Now I understand the situation.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.940
Darjeeling, eh? It smells great.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:55.240
Yeah. It goes wonderfully with apple pie.

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:59.870
You'd better believe you'll never
see me in an apron again, Kimi.

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:01.830
My, oh my, you can't mean that.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:05.750
That's the one and only thing I've looked
forward to in life. I am so sad.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:10.880
Yikes, sorry! I swear I'll
make this up to you later!

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:14.010
This apple-free apple pie is tasty.

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.880
Come on!

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:20.510
More pertinently, you should've
brought her to me from the start.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.020
Isn't a missing girl
suffering from amnesia

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:25.980
exactly the sort of thing
for a detective to handle?

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.980
True enough.

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:33.030
You said Alicia, right? You really don't
know your own full name or anything?

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:37.200
No, the fact that I'm 17 years old
as of this year is about all.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.030
Seven years old--I see.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.580
Seventeen!

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:44.120
Well, in reality, you must be
about 12 or 13.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:47.000
That's the sense I get from
the development of her calves.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:51.630
This is not the place for
showing off your peculiar fetishes.

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:56.680
Alicia, we'll take on the responsibility
of verifying your true identity.

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:59.260
But I'm not saying we'll do it for free.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:02.640
Hey, Siesta, we're going to
take money from a child?

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:06.690
That's irrelevant; a child still counts
as one human being, and what's more,

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:11.190
I believe nothing is as unreliable
as uncompensated good intentions.

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.280
I guess that's true.

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:15.650
What can I do, then?

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:20.410
Alicia, I want you to do the work
of a detective in my place.

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:23.120
The work of... a detective?

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:27.500
Siesta, whatever your intentions,
isn't that too heavy a burden?

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:30.420
That could be, but...

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:34.590
I get it. The legendary detective is
currently closed for business, right?

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:37.130
But in that case, having me
take on the detective role

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.680
and Alicia work as sidekick would be--

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:44.640
No, that doesn't... How can I put it?
You just have the face of a sidekick.

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:46.730
That's absurd.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:51.610
If you've accepted this, we'll commit to
covering your food, clothing, and shelter.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:56.110
But I'm not sure I have the confidence
to suddenly be a detective.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:59.860
If you become a detective, you can order
your sidekick around however you please.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:03.450
Hurray! I'll do it! I want to play
the role of legendary detective!

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.910
That was an appalling
negotiation I just watched.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:09.920
So, specifically, what type
of work should I--?

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:14.670
Our Jack the Ripper seems
to have been resurrected.

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:19.340
Fuubi-<i>san</i>? Why? I thought
you went back to Japan.

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:22.640
Yeah, I recalled some minor business
I had to take care of.

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:24.680
More to the point...

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:27.310
When did you two pop out a child?

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:29.680
--You need to get your eyes checked.
--You should get your eyes checked.

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:34.980
To backtrack, when you say our Jack
the Ripper's been resurrected...

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:39.570
Yup. Yesterday, another new victim
of heart harvesting was discovered.

00:21:39.570 --> 00:21:41.490
The M.O. also resembles
the previous cases.

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:45.780
That's madness...
That night, Cerberus was...

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:50.040
Hel.

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:56.460
Truth is, we have some information
that may be useful in pursuing her.

00:21:56.460 --> 00:22:00.590
It's still only a rumor,
but we're hearing that an object

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:03.890
that could lead to bringing down
SPES is here in the city.

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:10.430
We're hearing that people refer
to it as... the "Eye of Sapphire."
